Ctx: ksctl cte policies create > Synopsis

This operation creates a CTE Policy. While creating policy at least one Security-Rule or Key-Rule or LDT-Rule must be provided as a json blob, either via the command line, or via a file.
Local flags hints: CTEPolicyName (mandatory) : Name of the policy (string). PolicyType (mandatory) : Possible values are Standard , Cloud_Object_Storage,  LDT or IDT. Description (optional) : Optional description of the policy(string). NeverDeny (optional) : Flag to always permit operations in policy. By default it is disabled, enabled on learn mode activation. Supported in Standard or LDT type policy(boolean). --restrict-update-json-file (optional): To restrict the policy for modification. If its value enabled means user not able to modify the guarded policy.
JSON example for Security-Rule.
  [
    {
  "effect": "permit",
  "action": "all_ops",
  "partial_match": false,
  "resource_set_id": "LinuxResourceSet",
  "exclude_resource_set": true
    }
  ]
JSON example for Key-Rule/ DataTx-Rule.
  [
    {
  "policy_id": "",
  "order_number": 0,
  "key_id": "MyKey",
  "key_type": "name",
  "new_key_rule": true,
  "resource_set_id": "",
  "key_usage": ""
    }
  ]
JSON example for LDT-Rule.
  [
    {
  "resource_set_id": "TestResourceSet",
  "current_key": {
    "key_id": "clear_key",
    "key_type": "name",
    "key_usage": "ONLINE"
  },
  "transformation_key": {
    "key_id": "MyKey",
    "key_type": "name",
    "key_usage": "ONLINE"
  }
    }
  ]
JSON example for IDT-Rule.
  [
    {
  "current_key": "clear_key",
  "current_key_type": "name",
  "transformation_key": "MyKey",
  "transformation_key_type": "name"
    }
  ]
JSON example for RestrictUpdate {
  "restrict_update": false
} JSON example for Signature-Rule.
  [
    {
  "signature_set_id": "TestSignSet"
    }
  ]

```
ksctl cte policies create [flags]
```

Ctx: ksctl cte process-sets add-processes > Synopsis

This operation modifies a CTE ProcessSet.The parameters should be passed in as a json blob, either via the command line, or via a file. The JSON string should be constructed per the schema in the API Guide (CTE/ProcessSets section, PATCH to /v1/transparent-encryption/processsets/{id}/addprocesses).
 JSON string example:
    {
  "processes": [
  {
    "signature": "TestSignSet",
    "directory": "/home/testUser",
    "file": "*"
  },
  {
    "signature": "TestSignSet1",
    "directory": "/home/kyloTest",
    "file": "kylo.bin",
    "resource_set_id": "RS1"
  }
  ]
    }

```
ksctl cte process-sets add-processes [flags]
```

